jbbb+@andrew.cmu.edu (Joshua John Buergel) writes:
>>I have recently found this on the floor several times. What does it mean? or,
>>more importantly, what is it useful for?
>> 
>>Something is written here in the dust.  You read: "ad ?e?ar um".
>
>Spoiler Alert:


>This means that there is a secret door right next to this writing.  I
>never figured out exactly what it says, but it appears to be latin of
>some sort.  

"ad aerarium"  (sp?)  Means either, "to the gold" or "to the vault."

>At any rate, search the walls right next to where you find
>the message, and you'll find a secret door.  Ten to one it will be into
>a 'closet', or a pasage of only one place.  Odds are there will also be
>a trap in this closet, so searching for a while standing in the doorway
>is a good idea, usually.  Often it will be a teleportation trap that
>will put you into a vault on the level (if there is one).  Make sure you
>have some way to get out of the vault before you pop through.

Note that the chances are that if the trap is not a teleportation trap, it
is a *level* teleport trap...  It's very useful to have these around.

